00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:15.883
I think it's a mess.

00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:17.150
I think they need to start taking

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.750
and emptying their rubbish bins.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.850
I think they also need
to update your computers

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.120
'cause they look like
they're from the 90s.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.530
They need more ergonomical chairs.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.180
It's very boring and depressing.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.470
I wouldn't want to work there.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.890
Maybe that's why they're in the afterlife,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.141
because they've all died
because they work there.

00:00:34.141 --> 00:00:36.224
(laughs)

00:00:38.169 --> 00:00:40.160
Huh, actually don't mind it.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.130
I like as,

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.010
if you've watched Queer Eye,

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.920
you know I love a painted cabinet.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.020
It's a bit of a mess.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.170
I mean, it's a huge mess.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:49.070
It looks like the stove's falling apart.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.840
I'm not a huge fan of a
lavender robe on a dude.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.800
It just doesn't work for him.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.380
I mean to me, and if that's in 10 Downing,

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:59.810
I think it's very typical
of what it should look like,

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.050
which is exactly what
I would expect it to be

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:04.310
a little stuffy.

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.330
If I were to change it,
I would actually paint

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.540
it all white and then I would put some

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.260
super modern sofas in it because I love

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.810
mixing old and new together.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.310
I love taking old architecture

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.610
and making it all one color,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.913
but then putting in
modern furniture with it.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.980
Buckingham Palace, I
think that's beautiful.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.810
It's everything I'd hoped it would be.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.520
I want, love to go in there.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.580
Just so you know Netflix,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.707
you should take me to Buckingham Palace.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:31.810
It's beautiful.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.900
I mean, it is not my taste at all,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.090
but it's gorgeous.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:37.610
I can fully respect
different types of style

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.743
as long as they're beautiful.

00:01:39.743 --> 00:01:42.390
Oh that house looks just awful.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.570
It's awful, awful, awful.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.570
Her hair color's awful,
she needs to stop tanning.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.070
That's exactly what I would
expect in an old British house,

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.693
like floral curtains, yeah.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.020
That is, it's just sad.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.250
There was a trailer park down
the street where I grew up

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:00.250
called Lucky Lady Trailer Park

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.120
and I would always laugh
at there was really nothing

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.650
lucky about any lady
that had to live there.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:05.870
That's a pub?

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.683
It looks like a grandma's house.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.180
Yeah, no, I'm not a fan.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.230
I think it's a bit tacky.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.510
Again, floral curtains,
what's up with the floral?

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.490
Why would anyone put
curtains in a pub as well?

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.563
That's gotta stink.

